# VS Code Cheatsheet for HTML / CSS / JavaScript / TypeScript

A practical, frontend-focused reference for writing, navigating, formatting, debugging, and refactoring code in Visual Studio Code.

Shortcuts use the default Windows/Linux keymap (including Ubuntu). macOS equivalents are included where useful. Some features depend on extensions.

## 1. Essential shortcuts

These are the shortcuts you'll use most frequently while developing websites.

Command Palette

Find and run any VS Code command.

Ctrl + Shift + P

Quick Open

Open HTML, CSS, JS, or TS files by name.

Ctrl + P

Quick Fix

Apply code actions, fixes, and refactorings.

Ctrl + .

Format Document

Format the current file.

Shift + Alt + F

Go to Definition

Jump to a function, variable, or type definition.

F12

Integrated Terminal

Open a terminal for npm, Node.js, Git, and build tools.

Ctrl + `

